---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/ui/Breadcrumb.astro';
import '../styles/legal.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Acceptable Use & Anti-Fraud Policy - OTPWala"
  description="OTPWala's acceptable-use, anti-fraud, payment-integrity, and cooperation policy for temporary SMS verification services."
  canonical="https://otpwala.me/acceptable-use"
>
  <div class="legal-page">
    <section class="legal-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <Breadcrumb current="Acceptable Use & Anti-Fraud Policy" />
        <div class="legal-hero-badge">
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"/></svg>
          TRUST & SAFETY
        </div>
        <h1>Acceptable Use & Anti-Fraud Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-hero-sub">These rules protect users, payment partners, telecommunications providers, and the integrity of OTPWala.</p>
        <div class="legal-meta">
          <span><strong>Effective Date:</strong> September 17, 2026</span>
          <span class="meta-dot">&middot;</span>
          <span><strong>Last Updated:</strong> September 17, 2026</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="container legal-body">
      <div class="legal-layout">
        <aside class="legal-sidebar hide-mobile">
          <div class="legal-toc">
            <h4>Contents</h4>
            <nav>
              <a href="#purpose">Purpose and scope</a>
              <a href="#allowed">Allowed use</a>
              <a href="#prohibited">Prohibited use</a>
              <a href="#payments">Payment integrity</a>
              <a href="#monitoring">Monitoring and reviews</a>
              <a href="#reporting">Reporting abuse</a>
              <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
            </nav>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <article class="legal-content">
          <section id="purpose" class="legal-section">
            <h2>1. Purpose and Scope</h2>
            <p>This policy supplements the <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> and applies to every visitor, account, order, wallet transaction, referral, and support interaction on OTPWala. It does not replace the laws that apply to you or the rules of a third-party service you use.</p>
            <p>OTPWala provides temporary numbers for legitimate verification, testing, development, privacy, and other lawful purposes. A successful delivery does not mean a third-party platform permits a particular use.</p>
          </section>

          <section id="allowed" class="legal-section">
            <h2>2. Allowed Use</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>Lawful testing, development, quality assurance, and account verification where you have the right to create or access the account.</li>
              <li>Personal privacy protection and legitimate short-lived communication verification.</li>
              <li>Use that follows the terms, safety requirements, and applicable laws of the third-party service involved.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section id="prohibited" class="legal-section">
            <h2>3. Prohibited Use</h2>
            <p>You must not use OTPWala to facilitate, conceal, or attempt any of the following:</p>
            <ul class="danger-list">
              <li>Fraud, impersonation, phishing, extortion, identity theft, money laundering, terrorist financing, or evasion of sanctions.</li>
              <li>Unauthorized access, account takeover, ban evasion, fake reviews, deceptive registrations, or circumvention of a platform's security controls.</li>
              <li>Spam, bulk unsolicited messaging, harassment, threats, stalking, or automated account creation.</li>
              <li>Financial abuse, unauthorized payments, false payment evidence, payment reversal abuse, or referral farming.</li>
              <li>Illegal goods or services, exploitation, abuse of minors, or any activity that violates the law or another person's rights.</li>
              <li>Attacks against OTPWala or its providers, including scraping, credential attacks, malware, denial-of-service activity, or vulnerability exploitation.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section id="payments" class="legal-section highlight-box">
            <div class="box-tag"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="1" y="4" width="22" height="16" rx="2"/><line x1="1" y1="10" x2="23" y2="10"/></svg> PAYMENT INTEGRITY</div>
            <h2>4. Payment and Wallet Integrity</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>Only use a payment account, UPI handle, or Binance account that you are legally authorized to operate.</li>
              <li>Submit accurate payment references. Do not reuse a UTR or Binance Order ID, fabricate blockchain transaction hashes (TxID), upload altered receipts/screenshots, or claim a deposit that was not made. Such actions constitute payment fraud.</li>
              <li>Wallet balances are strictly for the account that received the verified payment and are non-transferable. Cryptocurrency (Binance Pay / USDT) deposits are immutable and strictly non-refundable upon transfer. Any manual reconciliation or balance adjustment is subject to the Terms of Service, applicable law, and network rules.</li>
              <li>For an unauthorized, duplicate, or incorrectly credited payment, contact <a href="mailto:support@otpwala.me">support@otpwala.me</a> promptly with the transaction reference (UTR or Binance Order ID). Never send a UPI PIN, card CVV, banking password, cryptocurrency private key, wallet seed phrase, or Binance login credentials.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section id="monitoring" class="legal-section">
            <h2>5. Monitoring, Holds, and Account Reviews</h2>
            <p>To prevent fraud and protect the service, we may use rate limits, device and network signals, duplicate-account checks, referral-abuse detection, payment reconciliation, order limits, and manual review. Details of detection methods are intentionally limited so they cannot be bypassed.</p>
            <p>We may pause an order, restrict wallet activity, request reasonable verification, or suspend an account while investigating suspicious conduct. We may preserve relevant records and disclose them to payment providers, service providers, regulators, law enforcement, or courts where legally required or permitted. Any funds held during a review will be handled according to applicable law and the outcome of the review.</p>
          </section>

          <section id="reporting" class="legal-section">
            <h2>6. Reporting Abuse or Security Issues</h2>
            <p>Report suspected fraud, stolen accounts, abusive use, payment mistakes, or security vulnerabilities as soon as possible. Include the affected order or transaction reference, dates, and a factual description. Do not include passwords, authentication codes, UPI PINs, card CVVs, cryptocurrency private keys, seed phrases, or other secrets.</p>
            <div class="contact-card">
              <strong>Trust & Safety Contact</strong><br/>
              <span>Email:</span> <a href="mailto:support@otpwala.me">support@otpwala.me</a><br/>
              <span>Support:</span> <a href="https://t.me/OTPWalaSupport" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@OTPWalaSupport</a><br/>
              <span>Help Center:</span> <a href="/contact">Contact Support Page</a>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="contact" class="legal-section">
            <h2>7. Contact and Related Policies</h2>
            <p>For account, privacy, or payment questions, contact support. See the <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> for the complete contract and the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for information handling, retention, and user rights.</p>
          </section>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
